==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lī'kən}}, {{IPA|/ˈlaɪkən/}}, {{SAMPA|/"laIk@n/}}
*: Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɪtʃən|-ɪtʃən]], [[Rhymes:English:-aɪkən|-aɪkən]]
* {{audio|en-uk-lichen.ogg|Audio (UK)}}

====Homophones====
* [[liken]]

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# Any of many [[symbiotic]] [[organism]]s, being [[association]]s of [[fungi]] and [[algae]]; often found as [[white]] or [[yellow]] [[patch]]es on old [[wall]]s, etc.

====Quotations====
* '''1894''' — [[w:Rudyard Kipling|Rudyard Kipling]], ''[[s:The Jungle Book|The Jungle Book]], Lukannon''
*: The Beaches of Lukannon–the winter wheat so tall– <br/>The dripping, crinkled '''lichens''', and the sea-fog drenching all!
* '''1895''' — [[w:H. G. Wells|H. G. Wells]], ''[[s:The Time Machine|The Time Machine]]'', ch XI
*: It was the same rich green that one sees on forest moss or on the '''lichen''' in caves: plants which like these grow in a perpetual twilight.
* '''1915''' — [[w:John Muir|John Muir]], ''[[s:Travels in Alaska|Travels in Alaska]]'', ch V
*: The nibble marks of the stone adze were still visible, though crusted over with scale '''lichens''' in most places.

